# Published archive keeps only lib/, example/, doc/, skills/, README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, and pubspec.yaml. Everything below is dev/CI/test
# tooling that must not ship to pub.dev.
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN IS ROOT-ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, deliberately.
# .pubignore uses gitignore semantics, where a bare `config/` matches a directory
# named `config` at ANY DEPTH — including `lib/src/config/`. That is not a
# hypothetical: the inherited unanchored list is why BOTH published
# diene_auth_engine releases (1.0.0 and 1.0.1) are structurally unusable. Their
# `lib/src/config/auth_engine_config.dart` was silently dropped from the archive
# while `lib/diene_auth_engine.dart` still `export`s it and two more files
# `import` it, so any consumer that touches the barrel fails to compile:
#   "Error: Type 'AuthEngineConfig' not found."
# Verified against both archives read live from pub.dev: 26 lib/*.dart files
# each, lib/src/config/ ABSENT from both, barrel export present in both.
#
# The same hazard applies to `test/` and `tool/` — a source directory named
# `lib/src/test/` or `lib/src/tool/` would vanish just as quietly. Anchoring
# makes these exclusions mean what they were written to mean. The companion
# assertion in scripts/validate/publish-archive.sh is the durable control: it
# proves every lib/ source actually reaches the archive rather than trusting this
# file to be read correctly.
/.claude/
/.dart_tool/
/.direnv/
/.github/
/.kagent/
/.kloop/
/config/
/coverage/
/docs/
/nix/
/openapi/
/scripts/
/tasks/
/test/
/tool/
/.coderabbit.yaml
/.envrc
/.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
/.markdownlint.json
/.prettierrc.yaml
/atomi_release.yaml
/codecov.yml
/flake.lock
/flake.nix
/swagger_parser.yaml
/Taskfile.yaml
/CLAUDE.md
/VERSION
